    "parts": [
      {
        "label": "Innate",
        "text": "Innate: Periodically, Malzahar gains Void Shift until he takes non-minion damage or negates a crowd control effect, to which it then lingers for 0.25 seconds before expiring.\n\nVoid Shift: Malzahar gains crowd control immunity and 90% damage reduction.",
        "leveling": [],
        "mechanics": [
          {
            "type": "cc-immune",
            "category": "defense",
            "wording": "crowd control immunity",
            "evidence": "Void Shift: Malzahar gains crowd control immunity and 90% damage reduction.",
            "conditional": false
          }
        ],
        "values": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Void Shift's cooldown refreshes whenever Malzahar takes non-minion damage or is affected by a crowd control effect, and resets upon respawning.",
        "leveling": [],
        "mechanics": [],
        "values": []
      }
    ],
    "custom": [],
    "notes": [
      "Void Shift will not resist allied crowd control nor will it be deactivated by them.",
      "Void Shift will not mitigate true damage but the buff will still be consumed.\n  - It does not deactivate against the Nexus Obelisk.",
      "Shields will take priority over Void Shift, but the buff is always consumed, even if the shield fully mitigates the damage.\n  - However, if Malzahar has a spell shield and is hit by an effect that isn't negated by the spell shield, then if the shield fully mitigates the damage, Void Shift will not be consumed.",
      "Spell shields take priority over Void Shift for abilities that contain a crowd control effect.",
      "Void Shift will specifically not deactivate if Malzahar eats Honeyfruit or is within a hostile Frozen Heart passive aura.",
      "Void Shift is special cased to prevent Chum the Waters, and Death Sentence from attaching to Malzahar."
    ]
  },
